  [doc [#
docs-src/site/voice.cxd — the docs-voice rules as data (RULED: DOCS-43,
DOCS-47, RS-30).

Two ratchets, each read by a step:

  [python]    scripts/gen_site/docs_voice_check.cx (`make docs-voice-check`,
              TEST_TARGETS). The docs speak for CX on its own identity, and
              name Python only where a reader arriving from it needs the
              bridge (the design's voice rule 4). The step counts the word
              (any case, whole word) in every served SOURCE — the landing
              page, the guide sections and the about page, the reference
              sources, the LLM templates, the dev pages — and holds each
              file to its row here: a file with no row must read ZERO; a file
              with a row may read at most its `allow=`, and when it reads
              LESS the step refuses too, naming the new count, so the number
              here is always the measured one and only ever moves down (a
              ratchet). The three bridge pages keep their rows for good; the
              rows carrying a wave number are the floors DOCS-49's later
              waves lower to zero, one page at a time.

  [fixtures]  scripts/gen_guide/snippet_check.cx (`make guide-snippets-check`).
              Every example on a new or re-voiced page is a [fixture id=]
              citation replayed byte-exact (DOCS-47); `floor=` is the number
              of citations the guide's sections carry — a [fixture] counts
              one, a [pair] counts two — and a wave that lowers it is refused.
              A wave that raises it raises the floor in the same change.
#]]

